@@ -0,0 +1,28 @@
+# Daily Grind
+
+Requires Node.js 22 or later. `npm start` serves the homepage and newsletter API
+on `PORT` (default 11222), using only Node built-ins. No build is needed.
+
+`POST /api/newsletter` accepts JSON or a standard URL-encoded form containing
+`email`. Valid signups are appended to `data/newsletter.ndjson` before success is
+returned. Set `NEWSLETTER_DATA_DIR` to a private, persistent writable directory in
+production. The server exposes only the homepage, stylesheet, and newsletter
+script; subscriber files are never served. This collects subscriptions; sending
+newsletter campaigns is a separate process.
+
+Deploy behind HTTPS and preserve the Node server's response headers.
+`Connection-Allowlist` permits only the response origin and
+`https://images.unsplash.com`, with redirects and WebRTC blocked by default.
+It is enforced on all responses, including script/worker responses. A restrictive
+CSP limits requests to this server and Unsplash images, blocks workers, and
+authorizes only the newsletter script with a fresh per-response nonce. Browsers
+without Connection-Allowlist support receive CSP protection, but CSP cannot
+cover all network channels such as WebRTC and top-level navigations.
+
+Policy reports go to the same-origin `/api/security-reports` endpoint, which
+consumes and discards bounded reports to avoid storing sensitive URLs. The form
+announces success and request failures, preserves the email for retry, and has a
+server-rendered response when JavaScript is unavailable.
+
+Verification for this change is limited to static checks. No browser checks,
+server startup, or imports of the server entrypoint were performed.
